{"type":"text","text":"All three HUD values found blind (differential search) and proven by write + screenshot; recorded and promoted to the ROM's mapping file.\n\n## Results — Super Mario Bros. (World), World 1-1\n\n| HUD value | RAM address | Encoding |\n|---|---|---|\n| **TIME** (level timer) | `$07F8`–`$07FA` | 3 decimal digits, one per byte: `$07F8`=hundreds, `$07F9`=tens, `$07FA`=ones. Counts down, HUD redraws each tick. |\n| **Coins** | `$07ED`(tens) + `$07EE`(ones) | 2 decimal digits, one per byte; value = `10*$07ED + $07EE`; a coin increments `$07EE` and carries into `$07ED`. HUD copies both bytes straight into digit tiles. |\n| **Score** | `$07DD`–`$07E2` | 6 decimal digits, one per byte, most significant first (`$07DD`=10⁶ place … `$07E2`=10¹); the ones digit is a hard-wired 0 and is not stored. |\n\n### How each was found and proven\n- **Timer:** standing still, two `decreased` diff rounds (23 → 10 survivors) kept `$07F9`/`$07FA`; a read of `$07F8`–`$07FA` gave `[3,3,6]` matching a displayed TIME. Proof screenshots: wrote `123` → TIME redrew to **119**; wrote `555` → TIME **551**, exactly the three bytes `[5,5,1]`.\n- **Coins:** the first ? block coin took the display 00→01 and `$07EE` 0→1. Proof screenshots: wrote `$07EE`=7 then grabbed the coin → **x08**; wrote `$07ED`=9,`$07EE`=0x10 and forced a redraw → the tens tile rendered `9` and the ones byte rendered as a **letter tile** (proving raw copy, not a computed split); wrote `$07ED`=0,`$07EE`=9 then grabbed a coin → `$07ED`=1,`$07EE`=0 and the HUD showed **x10** (carry proven).\n- **Score:** the +200 coin changed `$07E1` (the hundreds digit) by 2. Extent proof: wrote `$07DC`–`$07E3` = `1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8`, forced a redraw (time-up death), and the HUD showed **2345670** — only `$07DD`–`$07E2` appeared; `$07DC`(1) and `$07E3`(8) did not. `$07D7`–`$07DC` is the separate TOP-score display.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: the status bar only redraws on an event (a coin/points change, or the death/level-restart path), not every frame — so each proof had to trigger the game to change the value or force a restart.\n\n`promote_mappings` wrote all 3 to the ROM's mapping file (now 13 addresses); the imported reference was held back this session, so these came purely from the running game."}
